[2026-06-12T00:14:46.573Z] [INFO] 2026-06-12T00:14:46.573267Z  INFO session_loop{thread_id=019eb8cd-56e6-7be2-b717-d0b58b8e77b6}:submission_dispatch{otel.name="op.dispatch.user_input" submission.id="019eb8cd-5932-7e23-bc12-25c5bb1984ce" codex.op="user_input"}:turn{otel.name="session_task.turn" thread.id=019eb8cd-56e6-7be2-b717-d0b58b8e77b6 turn.id=019eb8cd-5932-7e23-bc12-25c5bb1984ce model=gpt-5.5 codex.turn.reasoning_effort=xhigh}: codex_core::stream_events_utils: ToolCall: exec_command {"cmd":"gh pr edit 1907 --repo link-assistant/hive-mind --body-file /dev/stdin <<'EOF'\n## Summary\n\nFixes #1901.\n\n- Treat Playwright MCP rows as available only when they are connected or enabled and not pending, disabled, failed, disconnected, timed out, or otherwise unavailable.\n- Show pending/unavailable Playwright MCP as not connected in `/version` and interactive `system.init` diagnostics when no `mcp__playwright__*` tools are exposed.\n- Repair missing default Claude/Codex Playwright MCP registrations at runtime when `@playwright/mcp` is installed, while leaving pending/custom rows untouched for diagnosis.\n- Harden `Dockerfile`, `Dockerfile.dind`, `coolify/Dockerfile`, and `scripts/verify-docker-image.sh` so Docker images verify Playwright CLI fallback, local `@playwright/mcp`, and healthy Claude/Codex MCP rows.\n- Document Docker MCP behavior, mounted `/home/box/.codex` override behavior, and the reviewer-referenced deployment gist in `docs/case-studies/issue-1901/`.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nBefore this change, output such as:\n\n```text\nplaywright: npx @playwright/mcp@latest - pending\n```\n\nwas treated as connected because the availability check only looked for the string `playwright`. The regression tests now verify that pending or bare Playwright rows remain unavailable, that connected/enabled rows pass, and that a missing registration is repaired only after the local MCP package is confirmed available.\n\nThe Docker follow-up also covers connected rows whose command contains `--timeout-action=600000`; that flag must not be mistaken for a `timeout` MCP status.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `npm run lint`\n- `npm run format:check`\n- `npx -y node@24 scripts/run-tests.mjs --suite default` (247 selected test files after merging `origin/main`)\n- `npx -y node@24 tests/test-issue-1901-playwright-mcp-pending.mjs`\n- `npx -y node@24 tests/test-docs-language-sync.mjs`\n- `npx -y node@24 tests/test-docker-dind-variant.mjs`\n- `npx -y node@24 tests/test-docker-release-order.mjs`\n- `npx -y node@24 tests/test-docker-box-migration.mjs`\n- Local runtime checks: `codex mcp list`, `claude mcp list`, `playwright --version`, `npx --no-install @playwright/mcp --help`\n- GitHub Actions run `27384178601` passed on `ce5a4d81`, including `docker-pr-check`.\n- GitHub Actions run `27385253934` passed on merged head `aaa60ae1`.\n\n`bash scripts/verify-docker-image.sh` was also attempted locally. It stopped before reaching the new MCP checks because this runner has pre-existing quiet Claude Code configuration drift in `/home/box/.claude/settings.json`; the direct MCP/CLI fallback checks above passed in the same environment.\n\n## Notes\n\nNo UI screenshots are included because this is CLI, Docker, and PR-comment behavior. The external case-study artifacts include downloaded CI logs, AI session logs, and the deployment gist used for the investigation.\nEOF","workdir":"/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1781216886121","yield_time_ms":10000,"max_output_tokens":12000} thread_id=019eb8cd-56e6-7be2-b717-d0b58b8e77b6
